    "created_at": "2020-12-20T15:13:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-20T15:13:11Z",
    "body": "Just a further thought on my implementation difficulties from above... I could maybe move encoding to be post-parse instead of pre-parse today.  That would let us still keep browser URL specifics out of the isolated library.  The main downside would then the library would need to operate on wide strings which creates other portability issues; WTF::String vs nsString, etc.",
