    "body": "Thanks for the update.\r\n\r\nI doubt we'll find a severe problem, but I will again point out: identifier encoding doesn't have \"LTR baked in\" because it works in terms of code points in logical order (it is `identifierStart`, not `identifierLeft` after all...). Maintaining the distinction can be helpful to you and others when answering requests such as the above.",
